<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/10/nvalt-update-rb.7539.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>
<p>nvALT is still a notes app. I don&rsquo;t intend to make it a fully-fledged Markdown editor. I already had a bunch of this written for the <a href="https://markedapp.com/help/Markdown_Dingus">Marked Dingus</a>, though, and once the code existed it was harder to leave it over there than to bring the useful parts across.</p>

<p>These all assume Markdown completion is the way you write. A few of the list tricks also want automatic list formatting turned on, which is the same switch nvALT has used for years.</p>

<h3 id="lists">Lists</h3>

<p>Option-Command-L cycles the current line. A plain line becomes a bullet, a bullet becomes a number, and a number goes back to plain text.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>buy milk</code></pre></div></div>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">*</span> buy milk</code></pre></div></div>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">1.</span> buy milk</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Tab and Shift-Tab indent and outdent a list item, a blockquote, or a selection of them. Control-Command-Left and Control-Command-Right indent ordinary lines. The width comes from the tab setting, tabs or spaces.</p>

<p>Numbered lists renumber themselves while you edit, including nested ones. Markdown highlighting colors list markers no matter how far they&rsquo;re indented.</p>

<p>Option-Command-L used to lock the note to the preview. That menu item is still there. It just doesn&rsquo;t have the shortcut anymore.</p>

<h3 id="quotes-fences-and-return">Quotes, fences, and Return</h3>

<p>Return on a blockquote continues the quote.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="gt">&gt; still quoting</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Return on an empty quote line drops the marker and leaves a blank line.</p>

<p>Return on the opening line of a code fence writes the closing fence and leaves the cursor on the blank line between them. Start with:</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">```</span><span class="nl">
</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Press Return and you get:</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">```</span><span class="nl">
</span>
<span class="p">```</span></code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id="links-and-footnotes">Links and footnotes</h3>

<p>Select some text and press Option-Command-K. nvALT wraps it in a Markdown link and parks the cursor between the parentheses.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">[</span><span class="nv">nvALT</span><span class="p">](</span><span class="sx">)</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Paste a URL onto a selection and you get the link filled in. Paste a URL by itself and it becomes an autolink, unless you&rsquo;re already inside a link or a reference definition, in which case you just get the URL.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">[</span><span class="nv">nvALT</span><span class="p">](</span><span class="sx">https://brettterpstra.com/projects/nvalt</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="nv">&lt;https://brettterpstra.com/projects/nvalt&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>F6 turns a selection into a reference link and adds the definition at the end of the note. Press it again on the marker to jump to the definition, or on the definition to jump back.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code><span class="p">[</span><span class="nv">the download</span><span class="p">][</span><span class="ss">1</span><span class="p">]</span>

<span class="p">[</span><span class="ss">1</span><span class="p">]:</span> <span class="sx">https://brettterpstra.com/projects/nvalt</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>F7 does the same job for footnotes. A selection becomes the footnote body. With nothing selected, the marker lands after the word under the cursor.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>Still a notes app.[^1]

<span class="p">[</span><span class="ss">^1</span><span class="p">]:</span> <span class="sx">I</span> mean it.</code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id="moving-and-selecting">Moving and selecting</h3>

<p>Control-Command-Up and Control-Command-Down move the current paragraph. On a list item, they move that item, including anything nested under it.</p>

<p>Option-Command-Up grows the selection by structure: the word, the inside of a pair of markers, the markers themselves, the sentence, the paragraph, the neighboring block, then the whole list, quote, or fence, and finally the note. Option-Command-Down walks back down.</p>

<h3 id="the-small-stuff">The small stuff</h3>

<p>Invisible characters and unusual spaces get a tint in the editor, so a line that looks empty and isn&rsquo;t will show itself. Zero-width characters, non-breaking spaces, that family of gremlins.</p>

<p>Keyboard Shortcuts opens in its own window now, instead of handing the file to another app.</p>

